# impeccable — vendored

Vendored so the detector travels with a clone of this repo, per §7 of the Verified
Launch tier process.

    Upstream   https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable
    Skill      v4.1.2
    Commit     5b585c0885a7c7d68523169b5b1934711794b80d (2026-09-01)
    License    Apache-2.0 — see LICENSE (and NOTICE.upstream.md for its own
               third-party attributions)

This is a copy of upstream's `.claude/skills/impeccable/`, plus the four
`impeccable-*` subagents in `.claude/agents/`. Nothing in it has been modified.
`package.json` is the only file added here — upstream declares these dependencies
at its own repo root, which a vendored copy does not inherit.

## Install once per machine

    cd .claude/skills/impeccable && npm install

`node_modules/` here is gitignored. `puppeteer` is optional and only needed for the
browser engine; the static-HTML engine used below does not require it.

## Run it

    node .claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/detect.mjs --json index.html

## DEGRADED is not a warning you can work around

If the run prints `DEGRADED`, **stop and install.** In degraded mode the detector
returns `[]`, which is indistinguishable from a clean pass. Measured upstream on a
real build: 0 findings degraded versus 5 installed; on a larger file, 7 versus 68.

**Never record a degraded run as a pass.**

## Verify findings before acting on them

Two classes are consistent false positives on these builds:

- `cramped-padding` on full-bleed sections whose inner `.wrap` carries the padding —
  measure it before touching anything (54–63px on past builds).
- `clipped-overflow-container` from `body { overflow-x: hidden }`.

It has caught real ones: an 11.2px label, an overused font, a cream ground, and a
flat type ramp.
